-They can't seem to
master these, yeah?

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:29.441
He looks like
he opened the fridge

00:13:29.441 --> 00:13:31.710
and can't decide what to eat.

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:39.084
"Activia.
Prunes. I don't know."

00:13:39.084 --> 00:13:41.086
It's not great, but can we
take a look at Trump's?

00:13:41.086 --> 00:13:44.189
Well, alright,

00:13:44.189 --> 00:13:47.592
maybe Biden's isn't so bad.

00:13:47.592 --> 00:13:49.995
Finally, on last night's episode
of "The Bachelorette,"

00:13:49.995 --> 00:13:53.632
there was a pretty interesting
scene between Katie and Mike P.

00:13:53.632 --> 00:13:55.734
We love "The Bachelorette"
here on the show.

00:13:55.734 --> 00:13:57.636
But those scenes
can get pretty emotional.

00:13:57.636 --> 00:13:58.770
So I thought that we could help.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.973
Here's a clip from
the episode re-voiced

00:14:00.973 --> 00:14:03.809
with the least-emotional person
we know -- Siri.

00:14:03.809 --> 00:14:06.478
This is "Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:14:06.478 --> 00:14:07.713
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:14:07.713 --> 00:14:09.414
-[ Whispering ]
"Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:14:09.414 --> 00:14:10.715
♪♪

00:14:10.715 --> 00:14:13.452
-"She is a nurturer,
and, man, do I love nurturers.

00:14:13.452 --> 00:14:15.754
She reminds me of my mom.
Your legs are soft."

00:14:15.754 --> 00:14:18.323
"Oh, well, thank you. Ha ha."

00:14:18.323 --> 00:14:20.625
My mom brings a nurturing touch
to everything

00:14:20.625 --> 00:14:23.295
and every situation
that she comes in contact with.

00:14:23.295 --> 00:14:24.729
Katie does the same thing."

00:14:24.729 --> 00:14:26.197
You remind me of my mom."

00:14:26.197 --> 00:14:28.433
-"Really?"

00:14:28.433 --> 00:14:30.235
-I wanna say congrats
to the Milwaukee Bucks

00:14:30.235 --> 00:14:32.237
for winning
their first NBA championship

00:14:32.237 --> 00:14:35.941
in 50 years.

00:14:35.941 --> 00:14:38.143
50 years.

00:14:38.143 --> 00:14:41.546
That's right, they beat
the Phoenix Suns 105 to 98,

00:14:41.546 --> 00:14:46.051
but of course, Arizona
has demanded a recount.

00:14:46.051 --> 00:14:49.955
The finals MVP was
Giannis Antetokounmpo

00:14:49.955 --> 00:14:51.689
who's from Greece.

00:14:51.689 --> 00:14:53.958
Yep, Greek NBA superstar.

00:14:53.958 --> 00:14:55.627
He could be the first person to
star in "Space Jam"

00:14:55.627 --> 00:14:58.263
and "Mamma Mia!"

00:14:58.263 --> 00:15:00.298
I love "Mamma Mia 2."

00:15:00.298 --> 00:15:03.201
Is that my boyfriend?

00:15:03.201 --> 00:15:06.004
Who? You mean, Fernando?

00:15:06.004 --> 00:15:08.707
Just setting it up.

00:15:08.707 --> 00:15:10.142
Last night's game was wild.

00:15:10.142 --> 00:15:14.312
The Bucks had 65,000 fans
watching from outside the arena.

00:15:14.312 --> 00:15:19.051
Look at this. Holy moly.

00:15:19.051 --> 00:15:21.786
Yeah, it was all fun and games
until 65,000 fans

00:15:21.786 --> 00:15:25.691
rushed to the one public
bathroom inside Starbucks.

00:15:25.691 --> 00:15:28.860
Well, today, President Biden
traveled to Cincinnati, Ohio,

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:31.430 line:0%
for a CNN town hall.

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:32.897
I'm not saying it was dull,

00:15:32.897 --> 00:15:37.135
but they used it to disperse
all the Bucks fans in Milwaukee.

00:15:37.135 --> 00:15:38.970
Speaking of the president,
a new poll found

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:42.141 line:0%
that 66% of Americans
approve of Biden's

00:15:42.141 --> 00:15:44.442 line:0%
handling of the coronavirus.

00:15:44.442 --> 00:15:47.146
The other 34% liked the way
things used to be back

00:15:47.146 --> 00:15:49.348
when we had to Clorox
wipe our bananas.

00:15:53.652 --> 00:15:56.622
Meanwhile, the Olympics
are just two days away,

00:15:56.622 --> 00:15:58.657
and I saw that due
to COVID concerns,

00:15:58.657 --> 00:16:02.193 line:0%
the U.S. women's gymnastics team
has left the Olympic Village

00:16:02.193 --> 00:16:05.030 line:0%
to stay at a nearby hotel.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:06.164
You know, there's a problem

00:16:06.164 --> 00:16:10.102
when Red Roof Inn
is the safer option.

00:16:10.102 --> 00:16:11.736
That's right,
the Olympics are almost here,

00:16:11.736 --> 00:16:13.939
and I saw that every sport
has its own unique

00:16:13.939 --> 00:16:15.774
logo designed for the games.

00:16:15.774 --> 00:16:18.343
For example,
here's tennis, yeah,

00:16:18.343 --> 00:16:20.045
well, it turns out while
these are the official logos

00:16:20.045 --> 00:16:21.479
for Olympic events,

00:16:21.479 --> 00:16:24.482
they're also the unofficial
logos for some other things.

00:16:24.482 --> 00:16:26.451
I'll show you what I mean.
Here's another logo.

00:16:26.451 --> 00:16:31.323
Officially, officially,
it's judo.

00:16:31.323 --> 00:16:34.026
Unofficially,
it's shopping at TJ Maxx.

00:16:37.796 --> 00:16:41.833
Here's another logo, officially,
it's wrestling, unofficially,

00:16:41.833 --> 00:16:44.003
it's someone
who lost a contact lens.

00:16:46.171 --> 00:16:47.505
And finally,
here's one last logo.

00:16:47.505 --> 00:16:50.743
Officially,
it's canoe sprint.

00:16:50.743 --> 00:16:52.477 line:0%
Unofficially,
it's a guy who regrets

00:16:52.477 --> 00:16:56.748 line:0%
renting a stand-up paddleboard
on vacation like.

00:16:56.748 --> 00:17:01.853
It looked cool in the picture.

00:17:01.853 --> 00:17:03.888
Some entertainment news,
CNN just announced

00:17:03.888 --> 00:17:06.291 line:0%
that they're launching
their own streaming service

00:17:06.291 --> 00:17:08.160 line:0%
called CNN+.

00:17:11.463 --> 00:17:14.132
Pretty sure there's already
a place to stream CNN 24 hours

00:17:14.132 --> 00:17:18.903
a day, it's called CNN, right,
am I missing something?

00:17:18.903 --> 00:17:21.639
Well, this isn't good, reports
of in-flight disturbances

00:17:21.639 --> 00:17:24.376
are up 500% this year,
in-flight disturbances.

00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:26.645
Now airlines are having to be
a little more aggressive

00:17:26.645 --> 00:17:29.180
and they're even
adjusting their slogans.

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:30.349
Take a look
at American Airlines's

00:17:30.349 --> 00:17:32.484
new slogan is,
"We duct taped a lady,

00:17:32.484 --> 00:17:35.453
don't think
we won't do it again."

00:17:35.453 --> 00:17:38.791
Oh, yeah, that's real.

00:17:38.791 --> 00:17:41.126
Also, Delta's new slogan
is now offering

00:17:41.126 --> 00:17:42.494
complimentary mouth guards.

00:17:42.494 --> 00:17:44.929
I mean, that's...
-Wow.

00:17:44.929 --> 00:17:46.864
And finally,
Frontier's new slogan is,

00:17:46.864 --> 00:17:48.299
we can't afford
to press charges,

00:17:48.299 --> 00:17:51.703
so do whatever, bro.

00:17:51.703 --> 00:17:54.072
Go for it.

00:17:54.072 --> 00:17:55.607
Well, get this,
Hidden Valley is now selling

00:17:55.607 --> 00:17:58.543
a one and a half pound tub

00:17:58.543 --> 00:18:00.745
of something called
pepperoni pizza dip.

00:18:00.745 --> 00:18:04.282
Check it out. Here's a photo.

00:18:04.282 --> 00:18:06.451
Proving once and for all that
some things from Hidden Valley

00:18:06.451 --> 00:18:09.588
should probably remain hidden.

00:18:09.588 --> 00:18:12.758
And finally,
today is National Hot Dog Day.

00:18:12.758 --> 00:18:15.393
-Wow.

00:18:15.393 --> 00:18:17.362
-How do I not lead with that?

00:18:17.362 --> 00:18:19.531
Today is National Hot Dog Day
to celebrate,

00:18:19.531 --> 00:18:22.301
Nathan's have five cent hotdogs
and for $1,

00:18:22.301 --> 00:18:23.735
7-Eleven
sells something cooked

00:18:23.735 --> 00:18:26.771
during the Obama administration.

00:18:26.771 --> 00:18:28.373
That's right,
it's National Hot Dog Day.

00:18:28.373 --> 00:18:30.975
So between that
and Jeff Bezos' rocket,

00:18:30.975 --> 00:18:34.579
what a week it's been
for phallic-shaped objects.

00:18:34.579 --> 00:18:35.714
Guess what's finally here.

00:18:35.714 --> 00:18:38.550
The summer Olympics
kick off tomorrow.

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:42.687
This is a big deal.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:18:42.687 --> 00:18:44.890
The official motto
for this year's Olympics

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:47.158
is "United by Emotion."

00:18:47.158 --> 00:18:48.961
Yeah, and
the unofficial motto is

00:18:48.961 --> 00:18:50.429
"As of right now,
we're still doing it."

00:18:50.429 --> 00:18:55.600
[ Laughter ]

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:57.135
That's right.
Tomorrow's the big day,

00:18:57.135 --> 00:18:59.738
and all of our best athletes
have arrived in Tokyo.

00:18:59.738 --> 00:19:02.574
Legends like Simone Biles,
Katie Ledecky...

00:19:02.574 --> 00:19:05.310
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:06.578
...Kevin Durant...

00:19:06.578 --> 00:19:08.013
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:19:08.013 --> 00:19:10.181
...and a dancing horse
named Butterscotch.

00:19:10.181 --> 00:19:12.283
[ Cheers ]

00:19:12.283 --> 00:19:14.920
Meanwhile, as if all the COVID
concerns around the Games

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:17.522
aren't bad enough,
a bear was spotted

00:19:17.522 --> 00:19:19.924
inside the softball stadium

00:19:19.924 --> 00:19:22.928
and is still on the loose.

00:19:22.928 --> 00:19:24.529
What an Olympics
this is gonna be.

00:19:24.529 --> 00:19:26.431
I mean, between the bears
and getting a disease,

00:19:26.431 --> 00:19:30.903
it's like we sent our athletes
to a game of "Oregon Trail."

00:19:30.903 --> 00:19:32.971
It's not a good situation.
Apparently, the bear got really

00:19:32.971 --> 00:19:36.441
agitated after officials made
him sleep on a cardboard bed.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:40.812
But officials are working hard
to make sure everyone stays safe

00:19:40.812 --> 00:19:42.581
and healthy
at this year's Games.

00:19:42.581 --> 00:19:44.916
But some people are still
unclear about what rules

00:19:44.916 --> 00:19:47.652
the athletes have to follow
in Olympic Village.

00:19:47.652 --> 00:19:51.489
So here to clear things up
is Olympics spokesman Ron Hobbs.

00:19:51.489 --> 00:19:56.394 line:0%
Ron?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:19:56.394 --> 00:19:58.663
Ron, what is the IOC's
official policy

00:19:58.663 --> 00:20:01.299
on getting together
and socializing in person?

00:20:01.299 --> 00:20:03.668
-Jimmy, we'd never tell
these world-class competitors

00:20:03.668 --> 00:20:05.337
what they can or can't do.

00:20:05.337 --> 00:20:06.772
We're simply discouraging people

00:20:06.772 --> 00:20:10.442
from engaging
in unnecessary physical contact.

00:20:10.442 --> 00:20:12.543
-Right.
Maybe you could clarify

00:20:12.543 --> 00:20:14.780
"unnecessary physical contact"?

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:16.715
-Simply put, no hanky-panky.

00:20:16.715 --> 00:20:17.883
[ Laughter ]

00:20:17.883 --> 00:20:20.785
No two-person push-ups.
No knocking boots.

00:20:20.785 --> 00:20:23.121
No boffing, boinking,
buttering the biscuits,

00:20:23.121 --> 00:20:26.390
boom-boom, bouncy-bouncy,
or bow-chicka-wow-wow.

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:29.327
-All right. Thank you.

00:20:29.327 --> 00:20:31.329
Is that -- Is that why the beds
are made of cardboard?

00:20:31.329 --> 00:20:32.731
-Actually,
the beds are just about

00:20:32.731 --> 00:20:34.199
sustainability and recycling.

00:20:34.199 --> 00:20:35.800
But if they happen to discourage

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:38.403
a game of human Tetris,
so be it.

00:20:38.403 --> 00:20:41.206
Because there should be
no grown-up nap time,

00:20:41.206 --> 00:20:44.542
no baking the potato,
no horizontal hula,

00:20:44.542 --> 00:20:46.911
glazing the doughnut,
greasing the loaf pan,

00:20:46.911 --> 00:20:49.081
or squat jumping
in the cucumber patch.

00:20:49.081 --> 00:20:52.050
-All right. I...

00:20:54.686 --> 00:20:56.288
I feel like
you're trying to say something

00:20:56.288 --> 00:20:58.089
without really saying it.
And that's...

00:20:58.089 --> 00:20:59.557
-Let me rephrase.

00:20:59.557 --> 00:21:01.293
No tangling the downstairs
Christmas lights.

00:21:01.293 --> 00:21:02.694
-Okay.

00:21:02.694 --> 00:21:06.198
-No ordering fries "animal
style" from "In-N-Out Burger."

00:21:08.967 --> 00:21:10.201
-What?

00:21:10.201 --> 00:21:11.770
Maybe you should just tell us

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.438
the full list
of what's not allowed.

00:21:13.438 --> 00:21:15.440
-Sure thing.
No rolling in the hay,

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:18.743
no digging up sand crabs,
no dipping the candle wick,

00:21:18.743 --> 00:21:21.245
sweeping the chimney,
opening the Gates of Mordor,

00:21:21.245 --> 00:21:23.415
letting the Joker
in the Batcave,

00:21:23.415 --> 00:21:25.884
doing the Monster Mash,
rummaging in the root cellar,

00:21:25.884 --> 00:21:28.253
searching for pocket change,
shocking the monkey,

00:21:28.253 --> 00:21:30.021
shrimping the barbie,
shucking the oyster,

00:21:30.021 --> 00:21:32.924
shellacking the canoe,
testing "the suspension,"

00:21:32.924 --> 00:21:35.661
battering the corn dog,
getting busy, getting down,

00:21:35.661 --> 00:21:37.462
getting it on,
getting some strange,

00:21:37.462 --> 00:21:39.998
getting some
stank on the hang down,

00:21:39.998 --> 00:21:42.267
doing "the nasty,"
"the wild thing,"

00:21:42.267 --> 00:21:45.771
or doing the hoody-hoo!

00:21:46.771 --> 00:21:51.142 line:0%
♪♪

00:21:51.142 --> 00:21:54.946
-Sorry. What I meant to say is,
what is allowed?

00:21:54.946 --> 00:21:56.981
-Well, uh,
hand stuff is fine.

00:21:56.981 --> 00:21:59.250
-Okay, thank you, Ron.

00:21:59.250 --> 00:22:00.819
Ron Hobbs, everyone.

00:22:00.819 --> 00:22:05.290
Thank you, very much.
Enjoy the Olympics.

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:09.694
-In-N-Out Burger.

00:22:09.694 --> 00:22:11.796
-Well, that's not all
people are confused about

00:22:11.796 --> 00:22:13.165
when it comes to the Olympics.

00:22:13.165 --> 00:22:14.866
There's a lot
of misinformation out there,

00:22:14.866 --> 00:22:16.801
so I thought it'd be helpful
to break down what's fact

00:22:16.801 --> 00:22:18.736
and what's fiction
about this year's Games.

00:22:18.736 --> 00:22:22.207
For example, Simone Biles
may attempt a Yurchenko

00:22:22.207 --> 00:22:25.810
double pike vault
and half-on with two twists.

00:22:25.810 --> 00:22:28.947
Fiction,
that's her Starbucks order.

00:22:28.947 --> 00:22:31.216
-It's not true.
-Yeah, it's not true.

00:22:31.216 --> 00:22:33.384
-Next up,
Facts -- karate, skateboarding,

00:22:33.384 --> 00:22:37.021
sport climbing, and surfing,
are making their Olympic debut.

00:22:37.021 --> 00:22:41.693
Fiction --
Frisbee golf is next, brah.

00:22:41.693 --> 00:22:44.362
And finally, fact -- the Games
will have no spectators.

00:22:44.362 --> 00:22:46.297
Fiction -- When they heard,
badminton players were like,

00:22:46.297 --> 00:22:48.800
"Wait.
You can have spectators?"

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:53.004
That's fiction.
They know that.

00:22:53.004 --> 00:22:55.774
Switching gears, last night,
Fox News aired a 10-second

00:22:55.774 --> 00:22:57.909
public-service announcement
urging viewers

00:22:57.909 --> 00:23:01.947
to get the vaccine.

00:23:01.947 --> 00:23:04.115
Although it didn't help when
they ended the PSA by saying,

00:23:04.115 --> 00:23:06.451
"Just so you know, this could be
the microchip talking."

00:23:06.451 --> 00:23:09.087
[ Laughter ]
[ Scattered "Oohs" ]

00:23:09.087 --> 00:23:11.556
[ Laughter ]

00:23:11.556 --> 00:23:15.226
Some tech news.
[ Chuckles ]

00:23:15.226 --> 00:23:17.962
I saw that Amazon --
Amazon's Alexa just rolled out

00:23:17.962 --> 00:23:23.468
a male voice assistant,
and his name is Ziggy.

00:23:23.468 --> 00:23:24.936
Right now,
Jeff Bezos is thinking,

00:23:24.936 --> 00:23:27.238
"I go to space for 11 minutes
and you name the voice Ziggy?

00:23:27.238 --> 00:23:29.340
What's going on?"

00:23:29.340 --> 00:23:31.709
Meanwhile, I heard that Twitter
is testing a new feature

00:23:31.709 --> 00:23:36.481
that lets users
upvote and downvote tweets.

00:23:36.481 --> 00:23:37.782
It's great.
It's like executives

00:23:37.782 --> 00:23:38.950
looked at Twitter and thought,

00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:42.654
"How can we make this place
even more toxic?"

00:23:42.654 --> 00:23:45.957
"Your grandma's 90th birthday?"
Enh!

00:23:45.957 --> 00:23:47.626
"No, thanks."

00:23:47.626 --> 00:23:49.594
Well, this isn't good.
I read that muffins

00:23:49.594 --> 00:23:52.730
sold at Walmart and 7-Eleven
have been recalled

00:23:52.730 --> 00:23:55.867
over concerns about listeria.

00:23:55.867 --> 00:23:58.402
Walmart apologized
while 7-Eleven just slapped on

00:23:58.402 --> 00:24:00.404
a sticker that said
"Listeria flavored."

00:24:00.404 --> 00:24:04.408
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:24:04.408 --> 00:24:09.347
"I'll take two of those."

00:24:09.347 --> 00:24:10.948
And, finally,
this is going viral.

00:24:10.948 --> 00:24:13.584
Teenagers in New Jersey
were celebrating a birthday

00:24:13.584 --> 00:24:16.387
on one of those slingshot rides
at an amusement park

00:24:16.387 --> 00:24:17.889
when something
unexpected happened.

00:24:17.889 --> 00:24:20.325
Watch this.

00:24:20.325 --> 00:24:22.394
-All right. Happy birthday.

00:24:22.394 --> 00:24:25.564
-Bye!
[ Screaming ]

00:24:32.369 --> 00:24:36.808
-What?!
-Wow!

00:24:36.808 --> 00:24:38.977
-What?!

00:24:43.781 --> 00:24:45.950
That girl will now go
through her life with a phobia

00:24:45.950 --> 00:24:48.052
of not just rides
but birthdays, in general,

00:24:48.052 --> 00:24:50.155
I mean, that's one of
the scariest things --

00:24:50.155 --> 00:24:52.089
Can we see that again?
That's insane.

00:24:52.089 --> 00:24:55.694
[ Both screaming ]
Oh, my God!

00:25:00.565 --> 00:25:02.367
Afterward, her friend was like

00:25:02.367 --> 00:25:05.570
"Yeah, we're definitely gonna
buy the photo from that ride."

00:25:05.570 --> 00:25:07.172
Well, guys, we are coming to you

00:25:07.172 --> 00:25:09.975
after the Olympic
opening ceremony right now.

00:25:13.011 --> 00:25:15.913
And a lot of people are talking
about Italy's outfits.

00:25:15.913 --> 00:25:17.515
Take a -- Take a look at these.

00:25:17.515 --> 00:25:19.217
Yeah.

00:25:19.217 --> 00:25:22.487
Look like a bunch of Sbarro
workers going on strike.

00:25:24.255 --> 00:25:27.792
Come on, Italy. You're in Japan,
the birth place of Nintendo.

00:25:27.792 --> 00:25:30.228
How can you not bust out
the Mario and Luigi overalls?

00:25:30.228 --> 00:25:32.596
I mean, come on.

00:25:32.596 --> 00:25:33.831
But this isn't good --

00:25:33.831 --> 00:25:36.101
an Australia equestrian athlete
was suspended

00:25:36.101 --> 00:25:39.170
for a positive cocaine test.

00:25:39.170 --> 00:25:41.872
Organizers knew something was up
when he jumped seven fences

00:25:41.872 --> 00:25:44.208
during practice and --

00:25:44.208 --> 00:25:47.579
and he wasn't on a horse.

00:25:49.247 --> 00:25:51.316
Some sports news here in
the U.S. --

00:25:51.316 --> 00:25:53.885
today, Cleveland announced
they're changing the name

00:25:53.885 --> 00:25:58.089 line:0%
of their baseball team to
the Cleveland Guardians.

00:25:59.491 --> 00:26:01.359
Come on, even the name
Washington Football Team

00:26:01.359 --> 00:26:03.895
is more exciting than that.

00:26:03.895 --> 00:26:05.763
I'm surprised they didn't go
with something more unique

00:26:05.763 --> 00:26:11.135
to Cleveland,
like The Layovers or...

00:26:11.135 --> 00:26:14.239
We Miss Lebrons. You know?

00:26:14.239 --> 00:26:16.341
People aren't wild about
their new logo either.

00:26:16.341 --> 00:26:17.408
Here, look at the logo.

00:26:17.408 --> 00:26:18.776
Oh.

00:26:18.776 --> 00:26:22.647
Looks like Thor's helmet hooked
up with Mr. Mets.

00:26:22.647 --> 00:26:23.681
So, this is big, too --

00:26:23.681 --> 00:26:25.049
the NFL announced that
this season,

00:26:25.049 --> 00:26:28.052 line:0%
teams will automatically forfeit
games that are delayed

00:26:28.052 --> 00:26:30.488 line:0%
by a COVID outbreak.

00:26:30.488 --> 00:26:32.524
Yup, the teams will have to
forfeit or worse,

00:26:32.524 --> 00:26:36.361
change their names to
The Guardians.

00:26:36.361 --> 00:26:38.596 line:0%
Some business news -- I saw that
Walmart is offering

00:26:38.596 --> 00:26:42.233 line:0%
free health screenings to
customers starting tomorrow.

00:26:42.233 --> 00:26:43.934
Meanwhile, one guy getting
his prostate checked

00:26:43.934 --> 00:26:45.670
at Walmart today is like,
"What do you mean,

00:26:45.670 --> 00:26:49.074
'starting tomorrow'?
Who are you?"

00:26:51.176 --> 00:26:52.911
Yeah, I have cash.

00:26:54.946 --> 00:26:57.648
And finally, I read about a mom
who threw her 6-year-old son

00:26:57.648 --> 00:27:02.019
a Southwest Airlines-themed
birthday party.

00:27:02.019 --> 00:27:04.188
His mom really nailed the theme,
because every kid went home

00:27:04.188 --> 00:27:07.025
with four ounces of water
and a bag of old potato chips.

